    "findings": [
      "The current rule stores only from/to/enabled/progress. Its editor offers change-disabled/change plus ongoing/complete; no independent automatic mode or per-imported-document override is represented.",
      "applyLinkedProgressRules runs only on active linked saved children after document/convert/purchasePlanGenerate, gathers actual allocations and applies an enabled rule. Plans use allocated row selections; other sources use document transition. It does not implement a general remaining-zero auto mode.",
      "Closed-PO protection precedes linked rules and closed-period protection follows them in the cloned command transaction. Existing tests already cover normal configured completion, explicit reopening and rejection of late reopening; these unchanged tests were not rerun.",
      "The existing plan-to-PO change rule is not reclassified as remaining-zero automatic change from the sales-order example. No global closure policy or stored setting is migrated."
    ]
  },
